{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 14, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a powerful ruler of the County of Tripoli during the 12th century. He ascended to the countship in 1183 succeeding his father Raymond II. His reign was marked by significant military campaigns political maneuvering and economic development within his domain. He is considered one of the most important rulers of the County of Tripoli.\n\n*Early Life and Ascendancy* Raymond III was born in 1145. He inherited the county at a young age a situation that presented considerable challenges. The county was a strategically important territory located on the Mediterranean coast facing threats from various powers including the Seljuk Turks and the Crusaders. Raymond III faced resistance from rival claimants to the throne and needed to consolidate his power to ensure the stability of Tripoli. He demonstrated shrewd political skills and a willingness to engage in diplomacy to achieve this. He also focused on strengthening the county's defenses building fortifications and improving its military capabilities.\n\nRaymond III’s reign saw increased interaction with the Crusader states. He maintained a complex relationship with the Kingdom of Jerusalem often engaging in both alliances and conflicts. He allied himself with the Crusaders to defend Tripoli against Seljuk incursions but also sometimes acted independently pursuing his own interests. This delicate balancing act was crucial for the survival of Tripoli in a volatile political landscape. He sought to expand the county's influence and control over surrounding territories.\n\n*Military Campaigns and Conflicts* Raymond III was a formidable military leader. He led several successful campaigns against the Seljuk Turks particularly in the Levant. These campaigns helped to secure Tripoli's borders and protect its trade routes. He also engaged in conflicts with other Crusader states and Muslim factions. His military successes solidified his position as a powerful ruler and enhanced the prestige of the County of Tripoli. He was known for his cavalry tactics and his ability to mobilize his forces effectively. He also implemented reforms to improve the county's army including training and equipping its soldiers.\n\n*Economic and Cultural Developments* Raymond III's reign fostered economic growth in Tripoli. He encouraged trade and attracted merchants from various parts of Europe and the Middle East. The county became a major center of commerce and a vital link between the East and West. He also supported the arts and culture promoting intellectual pursuits and attracting scholars to Tripoli. The city flourished as a center of learning and artistic expression. He oversaw improvements to the city's infrastructure including roads and harbors facilitating trade and communication. Raymond III’s legacy as a strong and capable ruler continues to be recognized by historians and scholars. He is remembered for his military prowess political acumen and contributions to the economic and cultural development of the County of Tripoli.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -0.1434580385684967}, {"token": "▁III", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Count", "logprob": -5.4834770708112046e-05}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -2.622600959512056e-06}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁was", "logprob": -0.09043829888105392}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.03864211589097977}, {"token": "▁powerful", "logprob": -0.5386373996734619}, {"token": "▁ruler", "logprob": -0.5502963066101074}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -0.8646833896636963}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.00048196621355600655}, {"token": "▁County", "logprob": -0.04307105019688606}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -1.6689160474925302e-05}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": -7.152555099310121e-07}, {"token": "▁during", "logprob": -0.2718907594680786}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.00